      "protected_subject": "authorization-authentication",
      "reason": "entrypoint.ts:24-25 honours ?x_astro_path whenever the client-sendable x-vercel-isr header equals '1', with no secret, and index.ts:453/474/499/703 bundle the same entry into _render; my Node v24.21.0 in-process run of the built head serverless-with-dynamic-routes _render (its chunk contains the x-vercel-isr check) returned {\"id\":\"public\"} without the header and {\"id\":\"private\"} with it for /api/public?x_astro_path=/api/private, which reopens the override that 335a20416 (#15959) removed; I could not measure production incidence because I have no platform access to see whether Vercel strips a client-supplied x-vercel-isr header."
    },
    {
      "#": 2,
      "status": "confirmed",
      "protected_subject": "authorization-authentication",
      "reason": "Running the built head fixtures/isr _isr function in-process with x-vercel-isr: 1, ?x_astro_path=/excluded/secret, /api and /two (all in isr.exclude, and config.json routes them to _render) rendered Dynamic, OK and Two with status 200, and got 404 without the header; entrypoint.ts:24-25 never checks the target against the ISR-eligible routes; I could not verify two platform steps offline: that a direct /_isr request is reachable through the handle:filesystem phase, and that Vercel sets x-vercel-isr on it."
    },
    {
      "#": 3,
      "status": "confirmed",
      "protected_subject": null,
      "reason": "test/isr.test.js only reads _isr.prerender-config.json and config.json routes, and path-override-security.test.js only calls _render without the header, so no test runs the _isr function; the diff adds no test, and my in-process run shows the built fixtures/isr _isr function returns 404 without x-vercel-isr and 200 <h1>One</h1> with it, so a regression in this branch would pass CI."
    }
  ]
}

